  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring Critical Protection Assistance for People On-The-Move and Strengthening National Disaster Management Capacities to Address Natural and Man-Made Threats in Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to address critical protection needs of vulnerable migrant returnees and internally displaced persons (IDPs), and strengthen the preparedness and response capacities of national authorities for improved risk management. The project is designed to strengthened emergency services for repatriated/deported Haitians and vulnerable returnees by improving protection assistance for IDPs suffering from urban gang violence; disaster preparedness and disaster risk reduction management capacities of key national institutions; health emergency response and mass casualty management capacities of the North department; and acute emergency response is supported in the event of a life-threatening natural or man-made emergency.</narrative>
  </description>
